> 
> No.  There is no water to walk on in the astrals.  

They're nice to have for the plane of fire, but the only advantage is 
that you don't need to take them off to pick up stuff or go down stairs 
or whatever. I would just use speed boots and a ring of levitation 
(especially if you ensure you have an extra or two).

>> I am using body armour(GDSM), I never miss when I attack with hands. Am
>> I losing damage by using armour? Is it worth it to wear body armour at
>> this point(it sure seems to be)?
> 
> I don't have an answer for you here.  If you hit Angels every time, then
> the Riders' AC is only one lower than them, so you'll probably be
> alright I guess, but I haven't done it myself so I can't speak from
> experience.

Body armor doesn't lower the damage you do, just your chance to hit 
(which is probably already astronomical). Leave it on. Also, you can 
probably do more damage with a weapon than hands; hands only average 
something like 9.5 dmg/attack, whereas a good artifact is up at 20/attack.

>> What should I do with my 4 wishes(I have already used wishes so not
>> going for conduct)? I think I may need more magic markers, and mabye
>> another wand of death. Am I missing anything that I need?
> 
> A ring of slow digestion wouldn't be a bad idea at all.  Apart from
> that, unless you're all out of magic marker it might be better to save
> the wishes for a rainy day.  

Get a blessed cockatrice corpse, if you're damn careful with it. I would 
wish it up right before waking Rodney; you don't want anything slowing 
you down after that, and 1-hit stonings help. I would also save one wish 
for the Astral plane (not the very last dust-making wish) for an emergency.

>> I really think this could be my first acsention, and I want to take it
>> slow and think it out. Is my experience level high enough? What about
>> my HP? I can revese genocide nurses or wraithes in sokoban again.
> 
> Most of that looks fine.  Do you have any potions of full healing
> around?  Definitely not a bad idea if you do, especially as a monk.
> 
Potions of full healing are by FAR the best way to raise your HP. If you 
know how to do alchemy, do that; each (blessed) !oFullHeal is worth 8 
max HP, and if you've been saving the right potions or willing to 
polypile, you can end up with 50+ of them. Keep about 10 for the riders.

> A third thing which isn't quite as crucial is a wand of secret door
> detection to find the door at moloch's sanctum.  You can just search the
> outer doors for it, but that's a minor pain.

You can use the Bell to do the same thing, if it has enough charges. You 
may have to search one or two walls manually.

> I'm sure I'm forgetting something.

Watch your HP. I tend to get used to never being hurt, and then when I 
get to the Astral plane I'll attack several times without checking my HP 
in between, and then when I look I can be down to 20%.

Scrolls of Earth are a decent (and lightweight) way of buying some time 
and can be used to trap dead Riders.

Save your teleport wands for Air, and once there never hesitate to use 
them. Air is the most critical plane to make quick; the rest of them 
pose little threat and even on Astral you have time to breathe so long 
as there isn't a Rider next to you.

Wands of death work on two of the Riders. Make sure to bounce the ray 
since they have a good chance to resist. There is no shame in a Helm of 
Opposite Alignment and it's a good reason to save a wish for the end.


